# SDD: Integration with existing kernel plan
status: active
authority: migration-integration
date: 2026-09-08

## Existing authority (do not overwrite)

- `.cronus/PLAN-2026-04-10.md` — **active**, kernel-only, language-focused.
- `LANGUAGE.md` — factual reality check (2026-04-10).
- `AGENTS.md` — agent cheatsheet; defers to LANGUAGE.md.

## Conflicts identified

| Kernel plan invariant | Migration pressure | Resolution |
|---|---|---|
| Scope is language, not a second product repo | We port *capabilities* into the language/renderer | Work stays inside `cronus-kernel`. Source `cronus-ui` is evidence-only. |
| `src/ui/**` has zero tests; layout/page recently rewritten | We must touch renderer | **Any** `src/ui` edit ships with regression tests in the same change |
| Dead server/router must not be patched | Easy to “fix” unused files | Forbidden. Live path is `main.rs::handle_request_inner` |
| `#![allow(dead_code)]` hid rot | Tempting to silence new code | Forbidden as a shortcut |
| Docs overstate `component` | Tempting to implement the documented Counter syntax first | Prefer smallest primitive catalog; do not implement docs-only React-like widgets as the first grammar |
| `compose` / `new` already exist | Master prompt suggests similar CLI names | New CLI verbs require a dedicated SDD; no name reuse without inventory |
| Single binary crate, no workspace | Design-system crate split | Stay one crate. Catalog is Rust modules + `.cronus` examples, not a new package |
| LANGUAGE.md last verified 2026-04-10 | We will change language | Update LANGUAGE.md only after REAL tests; bump the verified date |

## Integration rule

When PLAN-2026-04-10 and this migration disagree on *priority*, record the decision in `migration/SESSION-HANDOFF.md`. Default: **correctness of language + tests** wins over speed of UI port.

Do not archive or rewrite PLAN-2026-04-10 in this migration.
